From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bato <bato@local>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Wayland: survive pointers that come and go (no panic on a
 released wl_pointer, held buttons kept balanced, loop errors on stderr)

A wl_pointer released in remove_capability can still have events queued;
wayland-client rebuilds a dead proxy for them (no user data, version 0) and
`winit_data().expect(..)` panicked ("failed to get pointer data."). Those
events are dropped now, as are events of a pointer that is not the seat's
current one. When the pointer goes away over a window, its held buttons are
released and the cursor leaves. Held buttons are a set of codes, not a
counter. Dispatch/flush errors are printed (bato apps have no tracing
subscriber, so a protocol error used to end the app silently).

---
